<!-- Modal -->
<div class="modal fade" id="loginModal" tabindex="-1" role="dialog" aria-labelledby="loginModalLabel" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-dialog-centered modal-lg" role="document">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header">
        <h5 class="modal-title" id="loginModalLabel">Tabilet Login and Logout APIs</h5>
        <button type="button" class="close" data-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close">
          <span aria-hidden="true">&times;</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-body">

<h5>Page Returns HTTP Status Code 401</h5>
This means that the page is protected and a role login is required.
The response will contain the following headers.
<ul>
<li> <em>WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm="/app.php/ROLE/json/login", charset="UTF-8"</em><br/>
where <em>realm</em> shows the login endpoint.</li>
<li> <em>Tabilet-Error: CODE</em><br/>
This customized header gives a specific error code assigned by Tabilet.</li>
<li> <em>Tabilet-Error-Description: STRING</em><br/>
This customized header gives detailed error description.</li>
</ul>

<h5>Login at the Endpoint</h5>
To login, POST the credentials in body or in the Basic Authentication header
to the endpoint:
<p>
<samp>http://WEBSITE/app.php/ROLE/json/login</samp>
</p>
<p>
If the login fails, a HTTP 400 Status will be returned containing the following headers:
<ul>
<li> <em>Tabilet-Error: CODE</em>
<li> <em>Tabilet-Error-Description: STRING</em>
</ul>
</p>
If succeeds, the following raw JSON string will be returned:
<p><code class="language-json">{
	"token_type"   : "bearer",
	"access_token" : STRING,
	"expires_in"   : CODE
}
</code>
</p>
<p></p>
<h5>Navigations to Protected Pages</h5>
<p>
Logins via POST, which is the cases for web browsers, will get the token
in the Set-Cookie header as well, so the follow-up navigations will be seamless.
</p>
<p>
In API, you can send the token either in the Authorization
header or the POST body:
<ul>
<li> In header: <em>Authorization: Bearer [token]</em>
<li> In POST body: <em>STRING=[token]</em><br/>
where STRING is the name of the corresponding cookie, defined in <em>config.json</em>.
</ul>

<h5>Logout</h5>
To visit this endpoint will trigger logout:
<p>
<samp>http://WEBSITE/app.php/ROLE/json/logout</samp>
</p>
The response body will be 
<p><code class="language-json">{
	"success":true
}
</code>
</p>

      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer">
        <button type="button" class="btn btn-secondary" data-dismiss="modal">Close</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

